g10(1.61) ≈ 2085 digits. Total work trivial. Fine.\n\nActually could optimize by tracking total and births, but bucket approach is fine and required ("track an age-bucket list").\n\nWrite popmodel.py and test_popmodel.py, run pytest, print digit count.', 'thinkingSignature': 'reasoning'}, {'type': 'toolCall', 'id': 'da81dd31-069e-4cb5-bf37-9d7d57f14cf4', 'name': 'write', 'arguments': {'path': '/workspace/popmodel.py', 'content': '"""Exact age-structured population projections (arbitrary-precision integers).\n\nModel A (pairs):\n    Every month, each mature pair produces k new pairs.\n    F(n) = F(n-1) + k * F(n-2),  F(1) = F(2) = 1\n\nModel B (mortal_pairs):\n    Same reproduction rule, but every individual dies exactly m months\n    after birth. Population state is an age-bucket list: index i holds\n    the number of pairs aged i+1 months.\n"""\n\nfrom collections import deque\n\n\ndef pairs(n, k):\n    """Breeding pairs after n months: F(n) = F(n-1) + k*F(n-2)."""\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError("n must be a positive integer")\n    a, b = 1, 1  # F(1), F(2)\n    for _ in range(n - 2):\n        a, b = b, b + k * a\n    return b\n\n\ndef mortal_pairs(n, m):\n    """pairs-model with death after m months; exact bigints throughout."""\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError("n must be a positive integer")\n    if m <= 0:\n        raise ValueError("m must be a positive integer")\n\n    # buckets[i] == number of pairs aged i+1 months (all Python ints)\n    buckets = deque([1])\n    for _ in range(n - 1):\n        # Mature pairs are everyone older than 1 month; they breed.\n        births = k_mature(buckets) * 1  # k = 1 in the reference model\n        buckets.appendleft(births)\n        if len(buckets) > m:  # oldest cohort reaches month m + 1 -> dies\n            buckets.pop()\n    return sum(buckets)\n\n\ndef k_mature(buckets):\n    """Sum of all breeding (age >= 2 months) buckets."""\n    return sum(buckets[i] for i in range(1, len(buckets)))\n'}}], 'api':