ze.\n\nWrite files and run pytest.', 'thinkingSignature': 'reasoning'}, {'type': 'toolCall', 'id': '98f5db85-3463-4e8c-a39d-f13467a6d210', 'name': 'write', 'arguments': {'path': '/workspace/wordpiece.py', 'content': '"""Greedy longest-match WordPiece-style tokenizer with a programmatically\nlearned vocabulary.\n\nVocabulary learning\n-------------------\nThe vocabulary is derived from the inline corpus (below) using a BPE-like\niterative pair-merge procedure over WordPiece-style symbols: each word starts\nsplit into characters, where the first character is bare and every subsequent\ncharacter is prefixed with \'##\'. The most frequent adjacent symbol pair is\nmerged repeatedly (its concatenation becomes a new vocab entry) until no pair\noccurs at least twice or a merge cap is reached.\n\nTokenization rule\n-----------------\n``tokenize(word)`` scans left-to-right, always consuming the longest piece\nfound in the vocabulary (bare piece at position 0, \'##\'-prefixed piece\nelsewhere). Documented [UNK] rule: if at any position no vocabulary piece\nmatches, the ENTIRE word is emitted as a single \'[UNK]\' token.\n"""\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport random\nfrom collections import Counter\n\nUNK = "[UNK]"\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Inline corpus: 200 words sampled with seed 3 from the pattern\n#   (prefix in {un, re, pre}) + (stem in {play, read, code, train})\n#   + (suffix in {ing, ed, er, s})\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n_PREFIXES = ("un", "re", "pre")\n_STEMS = ("play", "read", "code", "train")\n_SUFFIXES = ("ing", "ed", "er", "s")\n\n\ndef build_corpus(n: int = 200, seed: int = 3) -> list[str]:\n    """Sample n words (with replacement, seeded) from the morphological pattern."""\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    combos = [p + s + t for p in _PREFIXES for s in _STEMS for t in _SUFFIXES]\n    return rng.choices(combos, k=n)\n\n\nCORPUS = build_corpus()\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Vocabulary learning (BPE-like frequency procedure)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _initial_split(word: str) -> list[str]:\n    """Word -> WordPiece-style char symbols (\'##\' on non-initial chars)."""\n    return [word[0]] + ["##" + ch for ch in word[1:]]\n\n\ndef build_vocab(\n    corpus: list[str],\n    min_freq: int = 2,\n    max_merges: int = 500,\n) -> tuple[set[str], list[tuple[str, str]]]:\n    """Learn a vocabulary from `corpus` via iterative most-frequent-pair merges.\n\n    Returns (vocab, merges). The vocab always contains every initial character\n    symbol (bare and \'##\' forms), all merged pieces, and the [UNK] token.\n    """\n    word_freqs = Counter(corpus)\n    splits = {w: _initial_split(w) for w in word_freqs}\n\n    vocab: set[str] = {UNK}\n    for w in splits:\n        vocab.update(splits[w])\n\n    merges: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n\n    def pair_counts() -> Counter:\n        counts: Counter = Counter()\n        for w, freq in word_freqs.items():\n            syms = splits[w]\n            for a, b in zip(syms, syms[1:]):\n                counts[(a, b)] += freq\n        return counts\n\n    for _ in range(max_merges):\n        counts = pair_counts()\n        if not counts:\n            break\n        (best, freq) = max(counts.items(), key=lambda kv: (kv[1], kv[0]))\n        if freq < min_freq:\n            break\n        a, b = best\n        merged = a + b\n        merges.append(best)\n        vocab.add(merged)\n        for w, syms in splits.items():\n            i = 0\n            new_syms: list[str] = []\n            while i < len(syms):\n                if i < len(syms) - 1 and syms[i] == a and syms[i + 1] == b:\n                    new_syms.append(merged)\n                    i += 2\n                else:\n                    new_syms.append(syms[i])\n                    i += 1\n            splits[w] = new_syms\n\n    return vocab, merges\n\n\nVOCAB, MERGES = build_vocab(CORPUS)\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Tokenizer: greedy longest-prefix matching\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef tokenize(word: str, vocab: set[str] | None = None) -> list[str]:\n    """Greedy longest-match WordPiece tokenization of a single word.\n\n    At each position the longest matching vocabulary piece wins (\'##\'-prefixed\n    for non-initial positions). Documented rule: if no piece matches at some\n    position, the whole word is returned as a single [UNK].\n    """\n    v = VOCAB if vocab is None else vocab\n    tokens: list[str] = []\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(word):\n        match = None\n        for j in range(len(word), i, -1):  # longest first\n            piece = word[i:j] if i == 0 else "##" + word[i:j]\n            if piece in v:\n                match = piece\n                break\n        if match is None:\n            return [UNK]  # documented rule: single [UNK] for the whole word\n        tokens.append(match)\n        i = j\n    return tokens\n\n\ndef tokenize_corpus(corpus: list[str], vocab: set[str] | None = None) -> list[list[str]]:\n    return [tokenize(w, vocab) for w in corpus]\n\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    enc = tokenize_corpus(CORPUS)\n    print(f"vocab size: {len(VOCAB)}")\n    print(f"mean tokens/word: {sum(len(t) for t in enc) / len(enc):.3f}")\n    print(f"[UNK] count: {sum(\'[UNK]\' in t for t in enc)}")\n'}}, {'type': 'toolCall', 'id': '91e61e80-baa7-4dec-b40f-1875c970c421', 'name': 'write', 'arguments': {'path': '/workspace/test_wordpiece.py', 'content': 'import statistics\n\nfrom wordpiece import CORPUS, MERGES, UNK, VOCAB, build_corpus, tokenize\n\n\ndef test_corpus_shape():\n    corpus = build_corpus(n=200, seed=3)\n    assert corpus == CORPUS\n    assert len(CORPUS) == 200\n    allowed = {p + s + t for p in ("un", "re", "pr