rror': False, 'timestamp': 1787568331408}}, {'type': 'message', 'id': '6d898b55', 'parentId': '713cd964', 'timestamp': '2026-08-24T10:45:41.373Z', 'message': {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'thinking', 'thinking': 'All green. One consideration: mean 1.015 means BPE merged nearly to whole words — legitimate but let me sanity check the greedy path still works on unseen combos (e.g., "repres"? not in pattern... "recodes" maybe). Not required. Done. Summarize briefly.', 'thinkingSignature': 'reasoning'}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'Done — all 7 tests pass.\n\n**`/workspace/wordpiece.py`**\n- **Corpus**: `build_corpus(n=200, seed=3)` samples with `random.Random(3)` from the 48 combinations of prefixes `{un, re, pre}` × stems `{play, read, code, train}` × suffixes `{ing, ed, er, s}`.\n- **Vocab**: `build_vocab()` runs a BPE-like frequency procedure — words are split into WordPiece-style char symbols (bare first char, `##` rest), and the most frequent adjacent pair is merged iteratively (deterministic tie-break by symbol pair) until no pair occurs ≥2 times. Result: vocab of 95 pieces including `[UNK]`.\n- **Tokenizer**: `tokenize(word)` does greedy longest-prefix matching (`##`-prefixed pieces for non-initial positions). Documented `[UNK]` rule: if no piece matches at any position, the whole word becomes a single `[UNK]`.\n\n**`/workspace/test_wordpiece.py`** verifies:\n1. Corpus shape (200 words, seed 3, pattern-derived, merges learned programmatically)\n2. Zero `[UNK]` across all corpus words + reassembly sanity check\n3. `"unplayable"` → single `[UNK]` (letter `b` never appears in the corpus, so no piece can cover it)\n4. Mean tokens-per-word = 1.015 ≤ 3.0\n5. Determinism (two full-corpus runs identical)\n\nOne bug caught during development: naive merge concatenation kept embedded `##` markers (`u##n`, `p##r##e`) which could never match during greedy scan; the fix normalizes each merged piece using the left symbol\'s continuation status.'}], 'api': 'openai-comp