 '2026-08-24T10:44:19.070Z', 'message': {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'thinking', 'thinking': "All green. Let me print the actual numbers to show measurable improvement, and also sanity-check Platt against sklearn's CalibratedClassifierCV-ish or just report numbers. Quick summary script.", 'thinkingSignature': 'reasoning'}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'All green. Let me print the actual measured numbers:'}, {'type': 'toolCall', 'id': 'b9ec3955-7bec-4020-ba4b-36c42c040518', 'name': 'bash', 'arguments': {'command': 'cd /workspace && python -c "\nimport numpy as np\nfrom calibrate import *\n_,_,p,y = make_overconfident_dataset()\nrng = np.random.default_rng(12345)\nidx = rng.permutation(len(y)); h = len(y)//2\nci, ei = idx[:h], idx[h:]\nscaled = platt_scale(p[ci], y[ci], p[ei])\nprint(f\'uncalibrated eval : ECE={expected_calibration_error(y[ei], p[ei]):.4f}  Brier={brier_score(y[ei], p[ei]):.4f}\')\nprint(f\'Platt-scaled eval : ECE={expected_calibration_error(y[ei], scaled):.4f}  Brier={brier_score(y[ei], scaled):.4f}\')\n"'}}], 'api': 'openai-completions', 'provider': 'openrouter', 'model': 'stealth/ox-alpha', 'usage': {'input': 258, 'output': 227, 'cacheRead': 5504, 'cacheWrite': 0, 'totalTokens': 5989, 'cost': {'input': 0.00019350000000000001, 'output': 0.0007945, 'cacheRead': 0.0008256, 'cacheWrite': 0, 'total': 0.0018135999999999998}}, 'stopReason': 'toolUse', 'timestamp': 1787568251829, 'responseId': 'gen-1787568251-rTdR5lo5ZEhJtWAov7zM'}}, {'type': 'message', 'id': '754b23bd', 'parentId': 'c7ccaa06', 'timestamp': '2026-08-24T10:44:19.638Z', 'message': {'role': 'toolResult', 'toolCallId': 'b9ec3955-7bec-4020-ba4b-36c42c040518', 'toolName': 'bash', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'uncalibrated eval : ECE=0.1313  Brier=0.1961\nPlatt-scaled eval : ECE=0.0104  Brier=0.1753\n'}], 'isError': False, 'timestamp': 1787568259638}}, {'type': 'message', 'id': '7916509d', 'parentId': '754b23bd', 'timestamp': '2026-08-24T10:44:30.090Z', 'message': {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': "Done — all 4 tests pass, with clear measurable improvement.\n\n## Files\n- **`/workspace/calibrate.py`** — the calibration library:\n  - `reliability_curve(y, p, n_bins=10)` — equal-width bins (last bin absorbs `p == 1`), returns mean predicted prob, observed positive fraction, and counts per bin\n  - `expected_calibration_error(...)` — ECE = Σ (n_b/N)·|mean_p_b − mean_y_b|\n  - `brier_score(y, p)` — mean squared error of predictions\n  - `platt_scale(cal_p, cal_y, eval_p)` — Platt's original formulation: fits `a + b·logit(p)` via BFGS on the logistic loss over held-out scores, applies to eval scores\n  - `make_overconfident_dataset()` — x ~ N(0, 1.5), true P = sigmoid(x), reported = sigmoid(2.5x), 20000 samples, seed 0\n\n- **`/workspace/test_calibrate.py`** — pytest suite with a module-scoped fixture doing a 50/50 calibration/eval split.\n\n## Results on the eval half\n\n| | ECE | Brier |\n|---|---|---|\n| Uncalibrated | 0.1313 | 0.1961 |\n| After Platt scaling | **0.0104** | **0.1753** |\n\nAssertions: uncalibrated ECE ≥ 0.05 ✓ · calibrated ECE ≤ 0.02 ✓ · Brier strictly improves ✓ · our Brier matches sklearn's `brier_score_loss` within 1e-12 ✓\n\nOne bug caught during iteration: my first ECE implementation took `|observed|` per bin instead of `|predicted − observed|`, which inflated ECE to ~0.50 and made it insensitive to calibration entirely — fixed to the correct gap term."}], 'api': 'openai-completions', 'provider': 'openrouter', 'model': 'stealth/ox-alpha', 'usage': {'input': 276, 'output': 409, 'cacheRead': 5760, 'cacheWrite': 0, 'totalTokens': 6445, 'cost': {'input': 0.00020700000000000002, 'output': 0.0014315, 'cacheRead': 0.000864, 'cacheWrite': 0, 'total': 0.0025025}}, 'stopReason': 'stop', 'timestamp': 1787568259639, 'responseId': 'gen-1787568259-w2IvFFarA4pqmn6FMB8X'}}], 'final_reasoning_content': None, 'final_content': "Done — all 4 tests pass, with clear measurable improvement.\n\n## Files\n- **`/workspace/calibrate.py`** — the calibration library:\n  - `reliability_curve(y, p, n_bins=10)` — equal-width bins (last bin absorbs `p == 1`), returns mean predicted prob, observed positive fraction, and counts per bin\n  - `expected_calibration_error(...)` — ECE = Σ (n_b/N)·|mean_p_b − mean_y_b|\n  - `brier_score(y, p)` — mean squared error of predictions\n  - `platt_scale(cal_p, cal_y, eval_p)` — Platt's original formulation: fits `a + b·logit(p)` via BFGS on the logistic loss over held-out scores, applies to eval scores\n  - `make_overconfident_dataset()` — x ~ N(0, 1.5), true P = sigmoid(x), reported = sigmoid(2.5x), 20000 samples, seed 0\n\n- **`/workspace/test_calibrate.py`** — pytest suite with a module-scoped fixture doing a 50/50 calibration/eval split.\n\n## Results on the eval half\n\n| | ECE | Brier |\n|---|---|---|\n| Uncalibrated | 0.1313 | 0.1961 |\n| After Platt scaling | **0.0104** | **0.1753** |\n\nAssertions: uncalibrated ECE ≥ 0.05 ✓ · calibrated ECE ≤ 0.02 ✓ · Brier strictly improves ✓ · our Brier matches sklearn's `brier_score_loss` within 1e-12 ✓\n\nOne bug caught during iteration: my first ECE implementation took `|observed|` per bin instead of `|predicted − observed|`, which inflated ECE to ~0.50 and made it insensitive to calibration entirely — fixed to the correct gap term."}) (input_keys={'filename', 'steps'}): [Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B] litellm.ServiceUnavailableError: ServiceUnavailableError: OpenAIException - Loading model
