d': '5b056fe4', 'timestamp': '2026-08-24T10:42:47.292Z', 'message': {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'thinking', 'thinking': 'Let me plan: create hashclf.py with HashingVectorizer-like class and SGD logistic regression, a corpus generator, and tests. Need to find an actual hash collision among tokens with 2^18 buckets — search for collision using the same hash function (e.g., Python\'s built-in hash? No — built-in hash is salted for strings across runs unless PYTHONHASHSEED set. Better use a deterministic hash like md5/sha1 or FNV-1a implemented manually). Use hashlib md5 of token bytes, take first 8 bytes as int, mod 2^18, sign = one bit. Deterministic across runs.\n\nCollision search: iterate generated tokens or synthetic tokens "w{i}" to find pair colliding mod 2^18. With 2^18=262144 buckets, birthday paradox: need ~600 tokens for good chance. Easy.\n\nSigned hashing: sign determined by another bit of hash. L2 normalize rows.\n\nSGD logistic regression: sparse-ish implementation using numpy arrays per document (indices, values), update weights only at nonzero indices. Or full dense weight vector of size 2^18 floats = 2MB, fine memory-wise. Dense weights are fine; "never materialize vocabulary dict" is about no token->index map. Dense weight vector 262144 * 8 bytes = ~2MB fine.\n\nImplement SGD with epochs, learning rate decay, L2 reg optional.\n\nCorpus generation: seed 4, 3000 docs, two classes with class-specific token distributions over 2000 synthetic tokens. E.g., vocabulary tokens t0..t1999; class 0 prefers even tokens, class 1 odd, with Poisson-ish doc lengths via rng. Make it separable enough but not trivially so—F1 >= 0.9 should be easy.\n\nMemory test: assert no attribute of model/vectorizer holds dict mapping str->int. Check all attributes recursively? Simple: assert not any(isinstance(v, dict) and v and all(isinstance(k,str) for k in v) for attribute values). Keep simple: check vectorizer and clf attributes for dict[str,int].\n\nTests: train/test split 30% test stratified-ish, compute F1 >= 0.9.\n\nFiles: hashclf.py, test_hashclf.py. Run pytest.\n\nWrite code:\n\nhashclf.py:\n\n```python\nimport hashlib\nimport numpy as np\n\nN_FEATURES = 2 ** 18\n\ndef _hash_token(token: str):\n    digest = hashlib.md5(token.encode("utf-8")).digest()\n    value = int.from_bytes(digest[:8], "little")\n    idx = value % N_FEATURES\n    sign = 1 if ((value >> 40) & 1) else -1\n    return idx, sign\n\nclass HashingVectorizer:\n    n_features = N_FEATURES\n    def transform(self, docs): return [self._doc(doc) ...]\n```\n\nReturn list of (indices, values) arrays. Also provide fit that does nothing (API compat).\n\nSGDClassifier:\n\n```python\nclass SGDLogisticRegression:\n    def __init__(self, n_features=N_FEATURES, lr=0.5, epochs=10, l2=1e-6, seed=0)\n    def fit(self, X, y): shuffle each epoch, for each doc compute z = w[idx]@vals + b, p=sigmoid(z), grad scale = (p - y); w[idx] -= lr*(grad*vals + l2*w[idx]); b -= lr*grad\n    def decision_function / predict\n```\n\nLearning rate schedule lr_t = lr0/(1+decay*t).\n\nCorpus generator in hashclf.py too (make_corpus). Tokens: f"tok_{i}" for i in range(2000). Class-specific distributions: class 0 samples from tokens where i%2==0 with probabilities from Dirichlet/rng.random normalized; class 1 odd similarly. Doc length rng.poisson(50)+5. Add some shared noise? Even/odd split gives perfect separability; maybe overlap slightly: 90% class-specific, 10% shared to make it non-trivial. Fine.\n\nCollision search function find_collision(tokens) returning pair. In test, generate candidate tokens until collision found, then verify _hash_token equal indices.\n\nf1_score implement manually.\n\nSplit: rng.permutation indices, 30% test.\n\nTrain accuracy should be high; F1 >= 0.9 easy.\n\nAlso test signed hashing reduces bias maybe not required. Requirements: F1 test, no-vocab test, collision unit test. Write and run.\n\nEdge: predict returns np array ints.\n\nLet me write files and run pytest.', 'thinkingSignature': 'reasoning'}, {'type': 'text', 'text': "I'll build this in three parts: the vectorizer + classifier + corpus in `hashclf.py`, pytest tests in `test_hashclf.py`, then run to green."}, {'type': 'toolCall', 'id': '3f50b612-bb9b-41fa-9cc2-784beb3202cf', 'name': 'write', 'arguments': {'path': 'hashclf.py', 'content': '"""Hashing-trick text classifier, from scratch (numpy only).\n\nComponents:\n- ``token_hash``: deterministic hash of a token -> (feature_index, sign).\n- ``HashingVectorizer``: maps documents to sparse L2-normalized feature\n  vectors using the hashing trick (feature index = hash(token) % 2**18,\n  signed hashing to reduce bias). No vocabulary is ever materialized.\n- ``SGDLogisticRegression``: binary logistic regression trained with\n  plain stochastic gradient descent on sparse batches.\n- ``make_corpus``: synthetic two-class corpus (class-specific token\n  distributions over 2000 synthetic tokens).\n"""\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nN_FEATURES = 2 ** 18\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Hashing\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef token_hash(token: str, n_features: int = N_FEATURES):\n    """Deterministically map a token to (index, sign).\n\n    Uses MD5 (stable across processes, unlike builtin ``hash`` which is\n    salted). The low bits of the first 8 bytes pick the bucket; a higher\n    bit picks the sign for signed hashing.\n    """\n    digest = hashlib.md5(token.encode("utf-8")).digest()\n    value = int.from_bytes(digest[:8], byteorder="little")\n    index = value % n_features\n    sign = 1 if ((value >> 40) & 1) else -1\n    return index, sign\n\n\ndef find_collision(candidate_tokens, n_features: int = N_FEATURES):\n    """Search candidates for two tokens that collide in feature index.\n\n    Returns ``(tok_a, tok_b, index)`` or raises RuntimeError.\n    """\n    seen = {}\n    for tok in candidate_tokens:\n        idx, _ = token_hash(tok, n_features)\n        if idx in seen:\n            return seen[idx], tok, idx\n        seen[idx] = tok\n    raise RuntimeError("no collision found in candidate tokens")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Vectorizer\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass HashingVectorizer:\n    """Hashing-trick vectorizer (sklearn-equivalent, hand written).\n\n    Never stores any token->index mapping; features are pure functions of\n    the token string.\n    """\n\n    def __init__(self, n_features: int = N_FEATURES, alternate_sign: bool = True,\n                 norm: str = "l2"):\n        self.n_features = n_features\n        self.alternate_sign = alternate_sign\n        self.norm = norm\n\n    def _encode_doc(self, doc: str):\n        tokens = doc.split()\n        counts = {}\n        for tok in tokens:\n            idx, sign = token_hash(tok, self.n_features)\n            if not self.alternate_sign:\n                sign = 1\n            counts[idx] = counts.get(idx, 0.0) + sign\n        if not counts:\n            return (np.empty(0, dtype=np.int64),\n                    np.empty(0, dtype=np.float64))\n        indices = np.fromiter(counts.keys(), dtype=np.int64, count=len(counts))\n        values = np.fromiter(counts.values(), dtype=np.float64, count=len(counts))\n        order = np.argsort(indices)\n        indices, values = indices[order], values[order]\n        if self.norm == "l2":\n            norm = np.sqrt(np.dot(values, values))\n            if norm > 0:\n                values = values / norm\n        return indices, values\n\n    def transform(self, docs):\n        return [self._encode_doc(d) for d in docs]\n\n    def fit_transform(self, docs):\n        # Stateless by design: fitting is a no-op.\n        return self.transform(docs)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Classifier\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass SGDLogisticRegression:\n    """Binary logistic regression trained with SGD on sparse rows."""\n\n    def __init__(self, n_features: int = N_FEATURES, lr: float = 0.5,\n                 epochs: int = 12, l2: float = 1e-6, seed: int = 0):\n        self.n_features = n_features\n        self.lr = lr\n        self.epochs = epochs\n        self.l2 = l2\n        self.seed = seed\n        self.coef_ = np.zeros(n_features, dtype=np.float64)\n        self.intercept_ = 0.0\n        self.t_ = 0\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _sigmoid(z):\n        return 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-np.clip(z, -60.0, 60.0)))\n\n    def _margin(self, indices, values):\n        z = self.intercept_\n        if indices.size:\n            z += float(np.dot(self.coef_[indices], values))\n        return z\n\n    def fit(self, X, y):\n        y = np.asarray(y, dtype=np.float64)\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(self.seed)\n        n = len(X)\n        order = np.arange(n)\n        for epoch in range(self.epochs):\n            rng.shuffle(order)\n            for i in order:\n                indices, values = X[i]\n                eta = self.lr / (1.0 + 1e-4 * self.t_)\n                self.t_ += 1\n                p = self._sigmoid(self._margin(indices, values))\n                err = p - y[i]\n                if indices.size:\n                    grad = err * values + self.l2 * self.coef_[indices]\n                    self.coef_[indices] -= eta * grad\n                self.intercept_ -= eta * err\n        return self\n\n    def decision_function(self, X):\n        return np.array([self._margin(idx, val) for idx, val in X])\n\n    def predict(self, X):\n        return (self.decision_function(X) >= 0.0).astype(np.int64)\n\n    def predict_proba(self, X):\n        return self._sigmoid(self.decision_function(X))\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Synthetic corpus\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef make_corpus(n_docs: int = 3000, vocab_size: int = 2000, seed: int = 4):\n    """Two-class corpus from class-specific token distributions.\n\n    Each class has its own distribution over ``vocab_size`` synthetic\n    tokens (with a small shared-noise component so the task is not\n    perfectly trivial). Returns (documents, labels).\n    """\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    vocab = np.array([f"tok_{i}" for i in range(vocab_size)])\n\n    # Class 0 favors even-index tokens, class 1 favors odd-index tokens;\n    # both share a small uniform background component.\n    even_mask = np.arange(vocab_size) % 2 == 0\n    base0 = np.where(even_mask, rng.random(vocab_size) + 0.5, 0.05)\n    base1 = np.where(even_mask, 0.05, rng.random(vocab_size) + 0.5)\n    p0 = base0 / base0.sum()\n    p1 = base1 / base1.sum()\n\n    docs, labels = [], []\n    for _ in range(n_docs):\n        label = int(rng.integers(0, 2))\n        dist = p0 if label == 0 else p1\n        # 85% class-specific draws + 15% uniform noise tokens.\n        n_specific = int(rng.integers(20, 61))\n        n_noise = max(1, n_specific // 6)\n        toks = list(rng.choice(vocab, size=n_specific, p=dist))\n        toks += list(rng.choice(vocab, size=n_noise))\n        rng.shuffle(toks)\n        docs.append(" ".join(toks))\n        labels.append(label)\n    return docs, np.array(labels, dtype=np.int64)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Metrics\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef f1_score(y_true, y_pred):\n    y_true = np.asarray(y_true)\n    y_pred = np.asarray(y_pred)\n    tp = int(np.sum((y_true == 1) & (y_pred == 1)))\n    fp = int(np.sum((y_true == 0) & (y_pred == 1)))\n    fn = int(np.sum((y_true == 1) & (y_pred == 0)))\n    if tp == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    precision = tp / (tp + fp)\n    recall = tp / (tp + fn)\n    return 2 * precision * recall / (precision + recall)\n\n\ndef train_test_split(docs, labels, test_size: float = 0.3, seed: int = 4):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    n = len(docs)\n    order = rng.permutation(n)\n    n_test = int(round(n * test_size))\n    test_idx, train_idx = order[:n_test], order[n_test:]\n    train_docs = [docs[i] for i in train_idx]\n    test_docs = [docs[i] for i in test_idx]\n    return train_docs, test_docs, labels[train_idx], labels[test_idx]\n'}}, {'type': 'toolCall', 'id': '7b3fc552-0528-4912-832b-dceb71a6f743', 'name': 'write', 'arguments': {'path': 'test_hashclf.py', 'content': 'import numpy as np\nimport pytest\n\nfrom hashclf import (\n    N_FEATURES,\n    SGDLogisticRegression,\n    HashingVectorizer,\n    f1_score,\n    find_collision,\n    make_corpus,\n    token_hash,\n    train_test_split,\n)\n\nVECTORIZER_ATTR_OBJECTS = None  # placeholder, computed lazily\n\n\ndef _iter_attr_objects(obj):\n    yield obj\n    for name in dir(obj):\n        if name.startswith("__"):\n            continue\n        try:\n            value = getattr(obj, name)\n        except Exception:\n            continue\n        yield value\n\n\ndef _find_vocab_dict(obj):\n    """Return any dict attribute that maps str -> int (a vocabulary)."""\n    for holder in _iter_attr_objects(obj):\n        for name in dir(holder):\n            if name.startswith("__"):\n                continue\n            try:\n                value = getattr(holder, name)\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n            if isinstance(value, dict) and len(value) > 0:\n                keys = list(value.keys())[:20]\n                if all(isinstance(k, str) for k in keys) and all(\n                    isinstance(v, int) for v in (value[k] for k in keys)\n                ):\n                    return f"{type(holder).__name__}.{name}"\n    return None\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope="module")\ndef fitted():\n    docs, labels = make_corpus(n_docs=3000, vocab_size=2000, seed=4)\n    X_train_docs, X_test_docs, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n        docs, labels, test_size=0.3, seed=4\n    )\n    vec = HashingVectorizer(n_features=N_FEATURES)\n    X_train = vec.transform(X_train_docs)\n    X_test = vec.transform(X_test_docs)\n    clf = SGDLogisticRegression(n_features=N_FEATURES, seed=0).fit(X_train, y_train)\n    return vec, clf, X_test, y_test\n\n\ndef test_f1_at_least_09_on_30pct_split(fitted):\n    _, clf, X_test, y_test = fitted\n    y_pred = clf.predict(X_test)\n    score = f1_score(y_test, y_pred)\n    print(f"test F1 = {score:.4f}")\n    assert score >= 0.9, f"F1 {score:.4f} below required 0.9"\n\n\ndef test_no_vocabulary_materialized(fitted):\n    """The model must never hold a token-to-index map (memory bound)."""\n    vec, clf, _, _ = fitted\n    assert _find_vocab_dict(vec) is None, "vectorizer materialized a vocab dict"\n    assert _find_vocab_dict(clf) is None, "model materialized a vocab dict"\n    # Weight storage is exactly n_features floats, nothing proportional\n    # to corpus vocabulary beyond that.\n    assert clf.coef_.shape == (N_FEATURES,)\n    assert clf.coef_.dtype == np.float64\n\n\ndef test_hash_collision_maps_to_same_index():\n    """Find two distinct tokens whose hashes collide and verify they\n    produce identical feature indices."""\n    candidates = (f"collision_probe_{i}" for i in range(1_000_000))\n    tok_a, tok_b, idx = find_collision(candidates, N_FEATURES)\n    assert tok_a != tok_b\n    ia, sa = token_hash(tok_a, N_FEATURES)\n    ib, sb = token_hash(tok_b, N_FEATURES)\n    print(f"collision: {tok_a!r} vs {tok_b!r} -> index {ia}")\n    assert ia == ib == idx\n    assert 0 <= ia < N_FEATURES\n\n\ndef test_vectorizer_output_is_l2_normalized_and_signed():\n    vec = HashingVectorizer(n_features=N_FEATURES)\n    doc = "alpha beta gamma alpha alpha delta epsilon zeta eta theta iota"\n    idx, val = vec._encode_doc(doc)\n    assert idx.dtype == np.int64\n    assert np.all(idx >= 0) and np.all(idx < N_FEATURES)\n    # L2 normalization\n    assert pytest.approx(np.sqrt(val @ val), abs=1e-12) == 1.0\n    # Signed hashing: some entries negative when multiple tokens collide\n    # into a bucket; single-token docs keep their sign.\n    idx1, val1 = vec._encode_doc("sometoken")\n    assert val1.size == 1 and val1[0] in (-1.0, 1.0)\n    # Repeated tokens accumulate before normalization.\n    idx2, val2 = vec._encode_doc("sometoken sometoken sometoken")\n    assert idx2[0] == idx1[0]\n    assert val2[0] == 3.0 * val1[0]\n\n\ndef test_pipeline_smoke_small_features():\n    """End-to-end sanity check on a tiny feature space."""\n    docs, labels = make_corpus(n_docs=200, vocab_size=50, seed=4)\n    vec = HashingVectorizer(n_features=256)\n    X = vec.transform(docs)\n    clf = SGDLogisticRegression(n_features=256, epochs=30, seed=0).fit(X, labels)\n    acc = np.mean(clf.predict(X) == labels)\n    assert acc > 0.9\n'}}], 'api': 'openai-completions', 'provider': 'openrouter', 'model': 'stealth/ox-alpha', 'usage': {'input': 212, 'output': 4037, 'cacheRead': 1344, 'cacheWrite': 0, 'totalTokens': 5593, 'cost': {'input': 0.00015900000000000002, 'output': 0.0141295, 'cacheRead': 0.0002016, 'cacheWrite': 0, 'total': 0.014490099999999999}}, 'stopReason': 'toolUse', 'timestamp': 1787568068997, 'responseId': 'gen-1787568069-aDsm5Ivg2h90qpo0MlCT'}}, {'type': 'message', 'id': '63813363', 'parentId': '20aa71ae', 'timestamp': '2026-08-24T10:42:47.300Z', 'message': {'role': 'toolResult', 'toolCallId': '3f50b612-bb9b-41fa-9cc2-784beb3202cf', 'toolName': 'write', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Successfully wrote 7939 bytes to hashclf.py'}], 'isError': False, 'timestamp': 1787568167300}}, {'type': 'message', 'id': '6532850d', 'parentId': '63813363', 'timestamp': '2026-08-24T10:42:47.301Z', 'message': {'role': 'toolResult', 'toolCallId': '7b3fc552-0528-4912-832b-dceb71a6f743', 'toolName': 'write', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Successfully wrote 41