nt:\n\n| Test | Requirement |\n|---|---|\n| `test_f1_at_least_09_on_30pct_split` | **F1 = 1.0000** ≥ 0.9 on the 30% split |\n| `test_no_vocabulary_materialized` | recursively inspects all attributes of vectorizer + model, asserts no `dict[str, int]` (token→index map) exists anywhere |\n| `test_hash_collision_maps_to_same_index` | searches candidates until birthday-paradox collision — found `collision_probe_483` vs `collision_probe_494` → both index **41505** — and verifies equality through `token_hash` directly |\n| `test_vectorizer_output_is_l2_normalized_and_signed` | unit norm, valid indices in `[0, 2¹⁸)`, signed values, count accumulation before normalization |\n| `test_pipeline_smoke_small_features` | end-to-end sanity check on tiny feature space |\n\n```\n5 passed in 1.08s\n```"}], 'api': 'openai-completions', 'provider': 'openrouter', 'model': 'stealth/ox-alpha', 'usage': {'input': 250, 'output': 517, 'cacheRead': 7616, 'cacheWrite': 0, 'totalTokens': 8383, 'cost': {'input': 0.0001875, 'output': 0.0018095, 'cacheRead': 0.0011424, 'cacheWrite': 0, 'total': 0.0031394}}, 'stopReason': 'stop', 'timestamp': 1787568219236, 'responseId': 'gen-1787568219-4Wojg7ChuE5jGqtb24nl'}}], 'final_reasoning_content': None, 'final_content': "All green. ✅\n\n## Summary\n\n**`hashclf.py`** — the from-scratch implementation (numpy only):\n\n- **`token_hash`** — deterministic MD5-based hash: `index = hash % 2**18`, sign taken from a high bit (**signed hashing** to reduce collision bias; MD5 because builtin `hash()` is salted per-process and wouldn't be testable).\n- **`HashingVectorizer`** — splits on whitespace, accumulates ±counts per bucket, then **L2-normalizes** each row. Emits sparse `(indices, values)` pairs. **No vocabulary dict is ever stored** — features are a pure function of the token string.\n- **`SGDLogisticRegression`** — logistic regression via plain SGD with inverse-time learning-rate decay, updating only nonzero indices per document (weights are a fixed 2¹⁸ float64 array ≈ 2 MB, independent of corpus vocab size).\n- **`make_corpus`** — 3000 docs, seed 4: two classes with class-specific distributions over 2000 synthetic tokens (`tok_0..tok_1999`, even-index favored by class 0, odd by class 1) plus 15% uniform noise so it's not trivial.\n- **`f1_score` / `train_test_split`** — hand-rolled metrics and 30% split.\n\n**`test_hashclf.py`** — 5 tests covering every requirement:\n\n| Test | Requirement |\n|---|---|\n| `test_f1_at_least_09_on_30pct_split` | **F1 = 1.0000** ≥ 0.9 on the 30% split |\n| `test_no_vocabulary_materialized` | recursively inspects all attributes of vectorizer + model, asserts no `dict[str, int]` (token→index map) exists anywhere |\n| `test_hash_collision_maps_to_same_index` | searches candidates until birthday-paradox collision — found `collision_probe_483` vs `collision_probe_494` → both index **41505** — and verifies equality through `token_hash` directly |\n| `test_vectorizer_output_is_l2_normalized_and_signed` | unit norm, valid indices in `[0, 2¹⁸)`, signed values, count accumulation before normalization |\n| `test_pipeline_smoke_small_features` | end-to-end sanity check on tiny feature space |\n\n```\n5 passed in 1.08s\n```"}) (input_keys={'filename', 'steps'}): [Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B] litellm.ServiceUnavailableError: ServiceUnavailableError: OpenAIException - Loading model
